Description: Patrone's desktop settings on the Desktop page
 With Patrone's taskbar installed, File Manager draws the desktop and
 Ubuntu's desktop icons and dock are off, so the page has Patrone's settings
 where Desktop Icons' were: where the desktop's files show, the corner of a
 clean desktop, and the Recycle Bin. It has no Dock settings either: their
 switches would bring Ubuntu's icons or dock back beside Patrone's.
Author: William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
---
--- a/panels/ubuntu/cc-ubuntu-panel.blp
+++ b/panels/ubuntu/cc-ubuntu-panel.blp
@@ -47,6 +47,38 @@
 
       Adw.PreferencesPage {
 
+        /* Patrone's desktop (its taskbar and File Manager), in place of
+         * Ubuntu's desktop icons */
+        Adw.PreferencesGroup patrone_desktop_group {
+          visible: false;
+
+          Adw.ComboRow patrone_files_row {
+            title: _("Desktop _Files");
+            subtitle: _("Where the files on your desktop show. A clean desktop keeps everything off it, the Recycle Bin too.");
+            use-underline: true;
+            model: StringList {
+              strings [
+                _("On the Desktop"),
+                _("In a Panel"),
+                _("Clean Desktop"),
+              ]
+            };
+          }
